<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Jamrud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1837</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghan-sikh-wars">Afghan–Sikh Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Jamrud was fought on 30 April 1837 at the fort of Jamrud, at the entrance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khyber-pass">Khyber Pass</a>, between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikh-empire">Sikh Empire</a> and an Afghan army sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dost-mohammad-khan">Dost Mohammad Khan</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sikhism">Sikh</a> general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hari-singh-nalwa">Hari Singh Nalwa</a> was killed, but the garrison held out until relief came, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghans">Afghans</a> withdrew. The battle confirmed Sikh control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peshawar">Peshawar</a> and marked the limit of Sikh expansion to the west.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-jamrud.jpg" alt="Battle of Jamrud" width="320" height="138" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Annie Brassey · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jamrud_Fort_-_pg_18_-The_last_voyage_-_Annie_Brassey.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
